{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Go to Pharaoh in the morning.</b> The custom of the king of Egypt, to this day, is to go out in Tammuz and Av, for then the Nile rises, to see how many levels it has risen. And HaShem commanded Moses to go in the morning and stand before the Nile and perform the sign, which is the plague of the Nile, before Pharaoh. And He commanded him to take the staff that turned into a serpent, by the hand of Moses, before his going to Pharaoh, and to give it to Aaron to stretch it over the waters of Egypt, so that Pharaoh would see with his own eyes — for from the moment Aaron strikes the Nile with the staff, it will turn to blood."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:23.348630943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}